{"id":"leetcode-543","version":1,"status":"approved","title":"Diameter of Binary Tree","summary":"Given the root node of a binary tree, calculate the longest path between any two nodes, measured by the number of edges.","statement":"Given the root node of a binary tree, calculate the longest path between any two nodes, measured by the number of edges.","constraints":["1–10,000 nodes; node values are in [-100, 100].","Measure path length in edges. The longest path need not pass through the root."],"topics":["trees","recursion"],"prerequisites":[],"signature":{"name":"tree_diameter","parameters":[{"name":"root","annotation":"TreeNode | None","adapter":"treenode","source_parameter":null}],"returns":"int","return_adapter":"raw","node_policy":"values","result_mode":"return","mutated_parameter":null,"immutable_parameters":[]},"starter_code":"# Data structure supplied to this problem.\nclass TreeNode:\n    def __init__(\n        self,\n        val: int = 0,\n        left: \"TreeNode | None\" = None,\n        right: \"TreeNode | None\" = None,\n    ):\n        self.val = val\n        self.left = left\n        self.right = right\n\n\ndef tree_diameter(root: TreeNode | None) -> int:\n    # Write your solution here.\n    pass\n","reference_solution":"def tree_diameter(root):\n    stack, heights, best = [(root, False)], {}, 0\n    while stack:\n        node, visited = stack.pop()\n        if node is None:\n            continue\n        if not visited:\n            stack.extend([(node, True), (node.right, False), (node.left, False)])\n        else:\n            left = heights.pop(node.left, 0)\n            right = heights.pop(node.right, 0)\n            best = max(best, left + right)\n            heights[node] = 1 + max(left, right)\n    return best\n","brute_force_solution":null,"known_wrong_solutions":["def tree_diameter(root):\n    stack, heights, best = [(root, False)], {}, 0\n    while stack:\n        node, visited = stack.pop()\n        if node is None:\n            continue\n        if not visited:\n            stack.extend([(node, True), (node.right, False), (node.left, False)])\n        else:\n            left = heights.pop(node.left, 0)\n            right = heights.pop(node.right, 0)\n            best = max(best, left + right + 1)\n            heights[node] = 1 + max(left, right)\n    return best\n","def tree_diameter(root):\n    stack, heights, best = [(root, False)], {}, 0\n    while stack:\n        node, visited = stack.pop()\n        if node is None:\n            continue\n        if not visited:\n            stack.extend([(node, True), (node.right, False), (node.left, False)])\n        else:\n            left = heights.pop(node.left, 0)\n            right = heights.pop(node.right, 0)\n            best = left + right\n            heights[node] = 1 + max(left, right)\n    return best\n"],"target_time_complexity":"O(n)","target_space_complexity":"O(h)","estimated_minutes":20,"rubric":{"algorithmic_insight":1,"prerequisites":1,"implementation":1,"performance_pressure":0,"edge_cases":0},"hints":["The longest path through a node joins its deepest left and right descendants.","Compute child heights before the parent and keep a separate global best path.","For each postorder node, update best with left_height+right_height, then return height 1+max(left_height,right_height).","The height returned to a parent and the best path anywhere in the tree are different quantities."],"editorial":"Postorder traversal makes both child heights available before a node is processed. Their sum is the number of edges in the longest path whose highest node is this node. Maximize that candidate over every node, not just the root. Return one plus the larger child height upward. The implementation uses explicit visited-state frames and discards child heights after use, so its auxiliary storage is O(h), without relying on Python recursion depth.","tests":[{"id":"lc-543-1","arguments":[[1,2,3,4,5]],"expected":3,"comparator":"exact","visible":true,"explanation":"The path 4→2→1→3 has three edges, which is maximal.","expected_node_order":null},{"id":"lc-543-2","arguments":[[1,2]],"expected":1,"comparator":"exact","visible":true,"explanation":"Two connected nodes have a path of one edge.","expected_node_order":null},{"id":"lc-543-3","arguments":[[0]],"expected":0,"comparator":"exact","visible":false,"explanation":null,"expected_node_order":null},{"id":"lc-543-4","arguments":[[-1]],"expected":0,"comparator":"exact","visible":false,"explanation":null,"expected_node_order":null},{"id":"lc-543-5","arguments":[[1,null,2]],"expected":1,"comparator":"exact","visible":false,"explanation":null,"expected_node_order":null},{"id":"lc-543-6","arguments":[[1,2,3]],"expected":2,"comparator":"exact","visible":false,"explanation":null,"expected_node_order":null},{"id":"lc-543-7","arguments":[[1,2,null,3]],"expected":2,"comparator":"exact","visible":false,"explanation":null,"expected_node_order":null},{"id":"lc-543-8","arguments":[[1,null,2,null,3]],"expected":2,"comparator":"exact","visible":false,"explanation":null,"expected_node_order":null},{"id":"lc-543-9","arguments":[[1,2,3,4]],"expected":3,"comparator":"exact","visible":false,"explanation":null,"expected_node_order":null},{"id":"lc-543-10","arguments":[[1,-2,3]],"expected":2,"comparator":"exact","visible":false,"explanation":null,"expected_node_order":null},{"id":"lc-543-11","arguments":[[0,0,0]],"expected":2,"comparator":"exact","visible":false,"explanation":null,"expected_node_order":null},{"id":"lc-543-12","arguments":[[1,2,null,3,4,5,null,null,6]],"expected":4,"comparator":"exact","visible":false,"explanation":null,"expected_node_order":null},{"id":"lc-543-13","arguments":[[1,2,3,null,4,5]],"expected":4,"comparator":"exact","visible":false,"explanation":null,"expected_node_order":null},{"id":"lc-543-14","arguments":[[7,7,7,7,7,7,7]],"expected":4,"comparator":"exact","visible":false,"explanation":null,"expected_node_order":null},{"id":"lc-543-stress-1","arguments":[[0,null,0,nu